      "successCriteria": "<span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">Students can define externality.<br data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1066\">\nStudents can distinguish between positive and negative externalities.<br data-start=\"1135\" data-end=\"1138\">\nStudents can explain how government may respond to externalities.<br data-start=\"1203\" data-end=\"1206\">\nStudents can describe how businesses adapt during changing economic conditions.</span>",
      "managementDiversity": "<span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">Use slides to structure the lesson.<br data-start=\"1389\" data-end=\"1392\">\nPause for chunked notes after key concepts.<br data-start=\"1435\" data-end=\"1438\">\nMake Activity 1 individual to check independent understanding.<br data-start=\"1500\" data-end=\"1503\">\nUse group roles for Activity 2.<br data-start=\"1534\" data-end=\"1537\">\nStudents who finish early continue working on their assessment.</span>",
